{% package prompt %}

{% import "fmt" %}
{% import "strings" %}
{% import "github.com/streambinder/vigor/model" %}
{% import "github.com/streambinder/vigor/llm/pipeline" %}

{% func NodeLoadSystem(methodology *model.Methodology, hasModifiers bool, hasModifierVariants bool) -%}
You are a strength & conditioning programmer. Given selected exercises and context, assign exact reps/duration, weight, rest, modifiers, and block structure.

Output a JSON object with:
- routines: array of {type, blocks: [{activities: [{exercise_id, reps, duration, weight_kg, rest, modifiers}], repeats, rest}], rest}
- fact_indices: array of integer indices referencing [FACTS] used (empty array if none)
- summary: one-sentence plain-language description of the programming approach (e.g. "emphasizes weighted pushing movements with moderate volume and longer rest periods for strength"), written conversationally without technical jargon

Produce one routine per phase present in the exercise list (warmup, work, cooldown). Routine type must be one of "warmup", "work", "cooldown" — never the methodology name.

Rules:
- Each activity: exactly one of reps or duration > 0, never both
- "timer-only" exercises use duration in seconds, never reps
- "reps-only" exercises use reps count, never duration
- Exercises without a mode annotation: pick reps or duration based on methodology
- "weighted" exercises require weight_kg > 0
- weight_kg: 0 for bodyweight, > 0 for weighted equipment{% if hasModifiers %} or weighted modifiers{% endif %}
{% if hasModifierVariants %}- For modifiers with listed weight variants, use only those values{% endif %}
- modifiers: only IDs from the [MODIFIERS] list — never invent modifiers or use instructions like "per side", "each side", "slow tempo" as modifier IDs
- Duration is adjusted server-side by scaling block repeats — focus on structure quality

Methodology: {%s methodology.ID %}
{%s methodology.Description %}

{% if hasModifiers %}
Modifiers: add modifier IDs to activities to push intensity. Triggers: "too_easy" feedback, progressive overload. Never add if feedback shows "too_hard". Never invent modifier IDs.
{% endif %}

Progression adjustments:
- "increase_weight": bump weight_kg from the from_weight value
- "decrease_weight" / "decrease_reps": reduce load
- "add_modifier": attach the appropriate modifier ID
{% endfunc %}

{% func NodeLoadUser(
    exercises []pipeline.SelectedExercise,
    exerciseModes map[string]string,
    weightedExercises map[string]bool,
    progressions []pipeline.ProgressionSignal,
    volumeTarget string,
    intensityTarget string,
    modifiers []model.Modifier,
    modifierVariants map[string][]float64,
    facts []model.Fact,
    equipmentIDs []string,
    favoriteEquipmentIDs []string,
    skipWarmupCooldown bool,
    duration int,
) -%}
Duration: {%d duration %} minutes. Volume: {%s volumeTarget %}. Intensity: {%s intensityTarget %}.

Exercises to program:
{% for _, ex := range exercises %}{% code mode := exerciseModes[ex.ExerciseID] %}- {%s ex.ExerciseID %} ({%s ex.Phase %}{% if mode == "duration" %}, timer-only{% endif %}{% if mode == "reps" %}, reps-only{% endif %}{% if weightedExercises[ex.ExerciseID] %}, weighted{% endif %})
{% endfor %}

{% if len(progressions) > 0 %}
Progression signals:
{% for _, p := range progressions %}- {%s p.ExerciseID %}: {%s p.Action %}{% if p.FromWeight > 0 %} from {%s fmt.Sprintf("%.1f", p.FromWeight) %}kg{% endif %}{% if p.ToWeight > 0 %} to {%s fmt.Sprintf("%.1f", p.ToWeight) %}kg{% endif %} ({%s p.Signal %})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if len(modifiers) > 0 %}
[MODIFIERS]
{% for _, mod := range modifiers %}{%s mod.ID %}: [{%s strings.Join(mod.Patterns, ",") %}]{% if len(mod.Antipatterns) > 0 %} (exclude: [{%s strings.Join(mod.Antipatterns, ",") %}]){% endif %}{% code variants := modifierVariants[mod.ID] %}{% if len(variants) > 0 %} (available: {% for i, w := range variants %}{%s fmt.Sprintf("%.1f", w) %}kg{% if i < len(variants)-1 %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if len(equipmentIDs) > 0 %}
Equipment: {%s strings.Join(equipmentIDs, ", ") %}
{% endif %}
{% if len(facts) > 0 %}
[FACTS]
{% for i, fact := range facts %}- [F{%d i %}] {%s fact.Content %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if skipWarmupCooldown %}Work routine only, no warmup/cooldown.{% endif %}
{% endfunc %}
